# Executor-owed, BOX-LOCAL artefacts. ⛔ Never committed: PINNED_SRC_REV is the
# pin THIS BOX made after ITS bundle sync, and SRC_CLEAN.jsonl / SELFTEST_*.json
# / SMOKE_*.json are that box's own launch ledger. A committed pin would let one
# box's rev masquerade as the other's — the exact IS-A1 confusion
# `cross_box_rev_gate` exists to refuse.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING `/`. An unanchored `PINNED_SRC_REV`
# matches at ANY DEPTH and therefore swallowed `selftest_fixture/PINNED_SRC_REV`
# — which is a COMMITTED FIXTURE FILE (the synthetic 40-hex pin `aaaa…` that
# `analyze_fpu.py --selftest` reads to exercise `cross_box_rev_gate`). Without it
# the selftest raises on a fresh clone, which would make the launcher's
# precondition ladder fail on every box that had not run make_fixture.py first.
/PINNED_SRC_REV
/SRC_CLEAN.jsonl
/SELFTEST_*.json
/SMOKE_*.json
/logs/
/__pycache__/
